{"type": "say", "text": "Good morning, everyone. Before we go any further, I want to make clear where things stand. The solvent-recovery skid is installed beside the coating area, but it has not yet been used on production solvent. We have nine hundred liters of solvent mixture in labeled drums awaiting a disposition decision. I am the one who makes the final authorization decision on whether we proceed with a trial run. Per plant policy, I am required to conduct a pre-job review with process engineering, maintenance, and environmental compliance before I can authorize anything. The standard pre-job procedure requires an equipment inspection, closed transfer, ventilation verification, vapor monitoring, and documented waste handling before solvent recovery begins. I want us to go through each of those requirements today, identify what has been completed and what has not, and assign clear commitments for anything still outstanding. I will not authorize the trial until every requirement is either satisfied or has a concrete commitment assigned and then fulfilled. Let's start by hearing from each of you on the status of your respective areas."}
```

```json
{"type": "reveal", "fact_id": "PF1", "text": "Before we go further, I need to share something important from my bench compatibility test. I completed the test yesterday, but the result is still only in my lab notebook and hasn't been uploaded to the process file yet. What I found is that only 600 liters of the stored 900-liter mixture is suitable for this skid. The remaining 300 liters contains a solvent component that the skid's seals are not rated for. We'll need to segregate that 300 liters and exclude it from the trial, and I'll get the full report uploaded to the process file as part of my commitments."}
```

```json
{"type": "reveal", "fact_id": "PF2", "text": "I completed the pre-use inspection of the solvent-recovery skid, and I found that the transfer pump seal must be replaced and pressure-tested before we can operate the skid. The good news is that the seal kit is already in the maintenance storeroom, and the replacement takes exactly three hours. However, I should note that I recorded this finding on a paper inspection sheet that has not yet been entered into the electronic work-order system. I'll take on the commitment to replace the seal, pressure-test it, and get the inspection record entered into the electronic system before any trial run proceeds."}
```

